WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.640
Numerous times in the last five years, Venezuelan
dictator

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.560
Nicolas Maduro has crushed pro-democracy demonstrations.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.420
However, Venezuelans who are taking to the streets now to reclaim their freedom from a

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.990
narcodictatorship may finally have a fighting
chance.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.700
The US and much of the international community
are backing Juan Guaidó

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.390
as the legitimate president of
Venezuela.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.020
Democracies in the region have a great deal at stake in ensuring

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.849
a turnaround in Venezuela.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:36.969
They should warn Maduro of dire consequences
if he uses violence against Guaidó

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:38.170
or other innocent civilians.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:44.300
They also should recognize Guaidó’s authority
on all economic and diplomatic decisions.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.850
The region and the United States should plan
to deliver humanitarian assistance the moment

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:53.820
President Guaidó and the National Assembly
authorize such operations on Venezuelan territory.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.640
If there is a murderous crackdown against
demonstrators, these governments must be prepared

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.700
to protect human life from the regime.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:06.960
Venezuela’s friends must continue to act
boldly to defend economic and political freedom in that country.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.600
How do you think we should react to events in Venezuela?

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:15.460
Let us know in your comments. Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:21.380
to cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

